const body = `<h1>1.7c — Dice Roller: Testing &amp; Integration</h1>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity rpg">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">RPG Build</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~15 min</span>
    </div>

    <h3>Testing Protocol</h3>

    <p>For each method in <code>Dice.java</code>, prove it works:</p>

    <ol>
        <li><strong>roll(sides):</strong> Call it 20 times for a d6. Record min
            and max. Did you ever get 0? Did you ever get 7?</li>
        <li><strong>rollDice(count, sides):</strong> Call rollDice(3, 6) 20 times.
            Verify: min >= 3, max <= 18, never outside range.</li>
        <li><strong>statRoll():</strong> Generate 6 stats (STR, DEX, CON, INT, WIS, CHA).
            Print them labeled. Verify each is in the 3–18 range.</li>
    </ol>

    <p><strong>Write your test results:</strong></p>
    <pre><code><span class="output">roll(6) test — 20 rolls:
Min: 1  Max: 6  (range correct? ✓/✗)

rollDice(3, 6) test — 20 rolls:
Min: ___  Max: ___  (range 3-18? ✓/✗)

statRoll() — 6 stats:
STR: 12  DEX: 8  CON: 15  INT: 11  WIS: 14  CHA: 9
All in range 3-18? ✓/✗</span></code></pre>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic Checkpoint</h3>
        <p>
            A classmate's <code>roll(20)</code> occasionally returns 0.
            Where is the bug? Walk through their formula step by step:
        </p>
        <pre><code>return (int) Math.random() * sides;</code></pre>
        <p>
            What's happening? Why does it always return 0? Can you explain the
            fix to them in plain English?
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="checklist">
        <h3>Checkpoint — before moving on, you must be able to:</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Systematically test every method you write — min, max, edge cases</li>
            <li>Explain why the parentheses bug in the random formula causes 0</li>
            <li>Generate a full set of RPG stats (3d6 for each of 6 attributes)</li>
            <li>Use a Dice.java utility class from another file (DiceTester.java)</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-01/dice-roller.html">Student RPG Guide: Dice Roller</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-01/math-random.html">Math.random()</a> — parentheses trap</li>
    </ul>
</div>`;
